>> title: Smoked Pork Ribs
>> category: Smoked & Grilled
>> tags: pork, ribs, barbecue, smoker, low and slow
>> counters: Smokehouse
>> aka: ribs, rib plate, St. Louis cut ribs, st louis ribs, spare ribs, spareribs, dry ribs, wet ribs, bbq ribs, barbeque ribs
>> servings: 4
>> time: 6 hr 15 min
>> pairs-with: memphis-dry-rub, barbecue-sauce
>> step.2: pull the membrane, rub
>> step.3: smoke 250°F (120°C) 3 hr
>> step.4: wrap, back in 2 hr
>> step.5: sauce for wet, dust with rub for dry, set 45 min

Bring the #smoker{} to 250°F (120°C) over hickory and hold it there.

Pull the membrane off the bone side of @St. Louis cut spare ribs{2%racks}(3 lb / 1.35 kg each) and rub them with @yellow mustard{1%Tbs}, @dark brown sugar{3%Tbs}, @smoked paprika{2%Tbs}, @kosher salt{1%Tbs}, @coarse black pepper{2%tsp}, @garlic powder{1%tsp}, and @cayenne{1/2%tsp}.

Smoke @&(~1)rubbed ribs{} bone side down for ~smoke{3%hr}, until the meat has pulled back from the tips of the bones.

Wrap @&(~1)ribs{} in #foil{} with @unsalted butter{4%Tbs}(55 g), @dark brown sugar{1/4%cup}(55 g), @honey{2%Tbs}, and @cider vinegar{2%Tbs}, and cook them back for ~smoke{2%hr}.

Unwrap @&(~1)wrapped ribs{}, brush them with @barbecue sauce{1/2%cup}(120 mL) for wet ribs or dust them with more rub for dry, and set the finish in the smoke for ~smoke{45%min}.
